1.	Prepare project introduction – Explain the project topic, background, and purpose.
	2.	Document requirements – Record the functional and non-functional requirements.
	3.	Document system design – Include architecture, flowcharts, diagrams, database design, and UI design.
	4.	Document development process – Explain the technologies, tools, and methods used.
	5.	Document testing – Include test cases, results, errors found, and corrections.
	6.	Add screenshots – Include important screens and features of the completed project.
	7.	Prepare user guide – Explain how users can operate the system.
	8.	Write conclusion and future scope – Describe the project outcome and possible future improvements.
	9.	Prepare references – List websites, books, research papers, and other resources used.
